  "turns": [
    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hi, it’s good to meet you. What brings you in today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S032",
      "patient_response": "I... well, I guess I'm here because things have just gotten to a point where I can't... I can't keep going like this. I do flooring for a living, you know, carpet, tile, lots of heavy installation work, and I have a crew who depend on me to keep the jobs lined up and keep things running smooth. I went to college for a couple of years before I got into the trades, so I've always prided myself on being the one holding it all together for them, and for my family at home. \n\nBut lately, I just... I've messed everything up so badly. I've let everyone down. And I just lay there in bed at night, and I keep thinking it would be so much better if I just didn't wake up. I really do. I just stare at the ceiling and think about how I'm ruining my family's lives, how I'm failing my crew, and sometimes I honestly feel like dying would be the fair punishment for what I've done to all of them. It just plays on a loop in my head, over and over, how they'd be better off if I just paid the price for the damage I've caused. I just want to go to sleep and not have to face them in the morning, because the guilt of what I've done to my crew and my family is just... it's too much. I don't deserve to be here.",
