    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Do you believe you have done something terrible that you should be punished for, even though other people tell you that isn’t true?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S030",
      "patient_response": "People say that, yeah. My husband, the guys on my crew... they try to tell me it's not true, that I'm just being too hard on myself or that I'm just going through a rough patch. But they're just being kind, or maybe they just don't want to admit the reality of it. Because I know exactly what I've done. \n\nI look at my husband, and I see how much worse he's gotten lately, how tired and just... drained he is all the time, and I know it's because of me. I'm the reason. I've dragged him down into this hole with me. And it's not just him. It's my crew, too. We had this great reputation, you know? Years of solid referrals for custom tile and carpet work. But I've caused them to lose work. I've ruined our chances on bids, or I couldn't get my head straight enough to organize the jobs right, and these guys—these guys who rely on me to put food on their families' tables—they are suffering because of my failures. \n\nAnd the jobs we actually did manage to do... I just keep thinking about the clients' homes. I know I messed them up. Even if the clients haven't called to complain yet, I know the work is tainted. It's like... it's honestly like I've poisoned everything I touched. Every person, every floor, every single house I stepped foot in. I just spread ruin everywhere I go. So when I say I should be punished, I'm not just saying it to be dramatic. I mean it. I deserve whatever happens to me. I deserve the absolute worst, because I'm the one who destroyed all of it, and no amount of them telling me otherwise is going to change the fact that I poisoned their lives.",
