    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Have you been hearing voices when no one is there?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S020",
      "patient_response": "I... yes. Yes, I have. It started a little while ago, and at first, I thought it was just the guys on the crew messing with me, or maybe just the noise of the tools, you know? Because when you're on a job site, there's always a saw running, or a compressor, or someone shouting over the radio. But then it kept happening when it was quiet. It's a man's voice. It's not my husband, it's not anyone on my crew... it's just this deep, clear voice. \n\nIt happens when I'm working, like when I'm kneeling down trying to line up a seam on a carpet, or laying out a tile pattern. I'll hear it right behind me, just over my shoulder. It says things like, 'You missed it.' Just that. 'You missed it.' And I'll stop what I'm doing and spin around, thinking one of the guys is standing right there pointing out a mistake I made, because God knows I'm making enough of them lately. But there's never anyone there. The room is completely empty. \n\nAnd it's not just at the job sites, either. It happens at home now. I'll be in the kitchen, just standing by the sink, trying to wash a dish or something, and I'll hear it again. Right behind my ear. 'Everyone knows.' That's what it says. 'Everyone knows.' And it's so real, Doctor. It's as clear as if you were standing right behind me speaking into my ear. I'll turn around, expecting someone to be standing right there in my kitchen, but I'm completely alone. It just... it makes my heart pound out of my chest, because I know he's right. Everyone does know how badly I've failed, but the fact that I'm hearing someone say it when the room is empty... I just don't understand what's happening to me. It's terrifying, honestly, because I can't escape it. No matter where I go, work or home, that voice is just waiting to remind me of what I've done.",
