    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Before this current period, have you ever had another episode like this in your life?",
      "targeted_symptom": "duration",
      "patient_response": "No, no, I've never... nothing like this. I mean, I've always been a worrier, sure, you know, making sure the bids are right, making sure the guys get paid on time, worrying about the house and the kids. But that was just normal stress, you know? Just the kind of stress anyone has when they're running a crew and trying to keep a family afloat. It was never like this. I've never felt this... this heavy, like I'm just dragging everyone down into the mud with me. And I certainly never heard a voice before. That's completely new. \n\nIt really all started... well, I can tell you exactly when it started. It's been about a year and five months now. That's when my husband had his accident. He hurt his back, really badly. We thought it was just a strain at first, you know, the kind of thing you just sleep off or put some ice on, but it wasn't. It was a serious injury, and it just... it completely changed everything. He went from being this active guy who was always doing things around the house, to being mostly housebound. He can barely get up from the couch some days without wincing. \n\nAnd that's when it all started falling apart for me. Because suddenly, everything was on my shoulders. I had to be the strong one, I had to keep the business running, I had to take care of him, and I just... I couldn't do it. I started feeling like I was failing him because I couldn't fix his back, and I was failing the crew because my head was at home worrying about him, and then the guilt just started piling up. So, yeah, it's been about a year and five months of this... this nightmare. Before that, I was fine. I was holding it all together. But since his injury, it's just been a steady slide down, and now... now I'm just ruining everything I touch.",
